etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4189661\nCREATED: 2026-06-13\nDOMAIN: scmp.com\nSLUG: why-japans-russia-outreach-could-fuel-g7-concern-over-unity-bad-signal\nTEXT: Japan\'s diplomatic outreach to Russia, led by Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi, has sparked concern among G7 nations over unity. The move comes as Japan seeks to boost energy cooperation with Moscow, a strategy that could make Europe "uncomfortable". Senior officials from Japan\'s foreign and trade ministries recently visited Moscow, where they held talks with Russian counterparts. This approach contrasts with the European Union and most Nato nations, who are united in their resolve to isolate Moscow over its aggression against Ukraine.\n\nID: 4189717\nCREATED: 2026-06-13\nDOMAIN: ibtimes.sg\nSLUG: japans-effort-protect-russian-lng-supplies-draws-attention-before-g7-gathering-87890\nTEXT: Japan is drawing attention with its efforts to protect Russian LNG supplies ahead of the G7 gathering. This move aims to maintain stability in global energy markets and prevent any appearance of fractures within the coalition supporting Ukraine. Japan\'s concerns are more focused on China and North Korea, but it also maintains a territorial dispute with Russia over the Northern Territories islands. This effort reflects Japan\'s long-standing goal of preventing a closer strategic alignment between Russia and China.\n\n\n',)
