etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4189521\nCREATED: 2026-06-13\nDOMAIN: channelnewsasia.com\nSLUG: lebanon-reports-strikes-south-israel-issues-broad-evacuation-warnings-6181136\nTEXT: Israel has issued broad evacuation warnings in southern Lebanon, with 24 locations affected, following a day of explosions and artillery shelling near the Ali Taher hills. The Israeli army warned residents to "evacuate your homes immediately and move to the north of the Zahrani River", approximately 45km from the southern border with Israel. Hezbollah has responded by launching drone attacks on Israeli military vehicles in the south, amid ongoing tensions between Israel and the Iran-backed group. Lebanon has reported over 3,700 civilian casualties due to Israel\'s airstrikes and ground invasion, while Hezbollah has rejected a conditional truce deal that requires it to cease attacks but makes no mention of Israel\'s actions.\n\nID: 4189169\nCREATED: 2026-06-13\nDOMAIN: hurriyetdailynews.com\nSLUG: lebanon-reports-israeli-strikes-in-south-after-evacuation-warning-223239\nTEXT: Lebanon reports Israeli strikes in south after evacuation warning. \n\nIsraeli strikes have hit the southern region of Lebanon, following an evacuation warning issued by the Lebanese government. The strikes occurred in the area near the border with Israel, where troops were evacuated earlier. \n\nThe Lebanese government has urged its citizens to remain calm and avoid traveling to the affected areas. The evacuation warning was issued after Israeli forces reportedly crossed into Lebanese territory, sparking a response from the Lebanese military. \n\nThe situation remains tense, with reports of damage and injuries in the affected areas.\n\nID: 4189241\nCREATED: 2026-06-13\nDOMAIN: gulftoday.ae\nSLUG: lebanon-reports-israeli-strikes-in-south-after-evacuation-warning\nTEXT: Lebanon reports Israeli strikes in south after evacuation warning. \n\nHizbollah fighters confronted Israeli forces advancing towards Majdal Zoun, amid ongoing conflict since March. Israel launched airstrikes and a ground invasion, killing over 3,700 people in Lebanon. \n\nA ceasefire deal announced this month failed to halt fighting, with Hizbollah rejecting direct talks and the conditional agreement. \n\nIran insists Lebanon must be part of any peace deal, while US officials say a deal with Iran includes Lebanon. \n\nLebanon\'s leaders accuse Tehran of treating the country as a "bargaining chip".\n\nID: 4189680\nCREATED: 2026-06-13\nDOMAIN: apnews.com\nSLUG: lebanon-israel-iran-hezbollah-7423a633aad2c74378e3024110af0a09\nTEXT: The Lebanese army withdrew its troops from a base in Kfar Tebnit after Israeli troops advanced nearby. Israel issued an evacuation warning for 20 locations, including Nabatiyeh and nearby villages. Airstrikes hit villages near Nabatiyeh, killing two people in Deir al-Zahrani. The Lebanese army moved its forces from the Kfar Tebnit barracks following an incursion by Israeli forces into the area, likely to capture strategic Ali Taher hill overlooking Nabatiyeh and nearby roads.\n\nID: 4189701\nCREATED: 2026-06-13\nDOMAIN: abc.net.au\nSLUG: 106794956\nTEXT: Israel has struck a city in south Lebanon, killing eight people and prompting the entire city to evacuate. The strike was carried out by Israeli forces in response to rocket attacks from Lebanon, which Israel views as a threat. The US and Iran have signaled that a peace deal is close, with Tehran claiming victory. However, Pakistan says the deal is within 24 hours of being finalized.\n\nID: 4189679\nCREATED: 2026-06-13\nDOMAIN: apnews.com\nSLUG: iran-war-us-pakistan-ceasefire-what-to-know-949710df39e3f1033cbb6beda3955814\nTEXT: Iran\'s demands for a ceasefire in Lebanon are tied to any potential deal with the US and Pakistan. Israeli Defense Minister Israel Katz stated that Israel could act independently towards Iran, but would not withdraw from occupied zones in Lebanon, Syria, and Gaza. Fighting continued in southern Lebanon on Saturday, with no clear resolution to the conflict.\n\n\n',)
