etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4189080\nCREATED: 2026-06-13\nDOMAIN: ibtimes.sg\nSLUG: us-orders-global-lockout-anthropics-fable-5-mythos-5-forcing-sudden-shutdown-too-powerful-87879\nTEXT: The US government has issued an export control directive to suspend all access to Anthropic\'s Fable 5 and Mythos 5 AI models, forcing a sudden shutdown. The company has apologized to customers, citing a "misunderstanding", and pledged to work towards restoring access as quickly as possible. This move comes amid growing tensions between Anthropic and the Trump administration, who are already engaged in a dispute over government use of the company\'s AI technology. The shutdown is also linked to criticism from researchers and startup founders who said Anthropic was restricting advanced AI research.\n\nID: 4189053\nCREATED: 2026-06-13\nDOMAIN: cbs8.com\nSLUG: 507-052e3003-12f3-421f-b57e-4cf446975882\nTEXT: The US Department of Commerce has added Anthropic Fable to its Entity List, effectively making the company\'s AI-powered technology unavailable for export. This move comes as a result of Anthropic Fable\'s alleged ties to the Chinese military, with some reports suggesting that the company\'s technology could be used for surveillance purposes. The new export controls aim to restrict Anthropic Fable\'s ability to sell its technology to entities on the US Entity List, effectively cutting off its access to international markets.\n\nID: 4189619\nCREATED: 2026-06-13\nDOMAIN: fakti.bg\nSLUG: 1060785-us-blocks-foreign-access-to-cutting-edge-artificial-intelligence-models\nTEXT: The US has blocked foreign access to cutting-edge artificial intelligence models, specifically the Mythos 5 and Fable 5 models. Commerce Secretary Howard Lutnick announced in a letter to Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei that these models will be subject to export controls, both outside the US and for foreign nationals within the country. This decision came after reports emerged that Mythos had been hacked, raising concerns about a potential threat to national security. Both models will remain restricted for several more weeks.\n\nID: 4189044\nCREATED: 2026-06-13\nDOMAIN: abc.net.au\nSLUG: 106794456\nTEXT: Anthropic ordered to halt foreign access to AI models. \n\nThe US-based company Anthropic has been instructed by a federal judge to immediately halt foreign access to its AI models. The order was made in response to concerns over the potential misuse of these models, which are used for tasks such as language translation and text analysis. The company\'s AI models have been the subject of scrutiny due to their potential for military and intelligence applications.\n\nID: 4189872\nCREATED: 2026-06-13\nDOMAIN: interestingengineering.com\nSLUG: anthropic-blocks-international-users\nTEXT: The US government has labeled top AI models, including Fable 5 and Mythos 5, as a national security risk due to their cutting-edge capabilities. Anthropic, the developers of these models, have limited access to them for international users, citing concerns over their strategic sensitivity. This move aims to prevent the misuse of advanced AI technologies by foreign entities, highlighting the growing importance of AI security in modern defense.\n\nID: 4189092\nCREATED: 2026-06-13\nDOMAIN: ibtimes.sg\nSLUG: anthropics-fable-5-restrictions-explained-what-new-u-s-ai-rules-mean-87874\nTEXT: The US government has introduced new AI rules, specifically targeting highly capable models like Anthropic\'s Fable 5. Officials are concerned that bypassing safety guardrails could accelerate offensive cyber operations, potentially leading to a "jailbreak" that allows users to exploit Fable 5\'s vulnerability identification capability. This could be used to target critical infrastructure, financial institutions, and government networks.\n\n\n',)
