etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4189557\nCREATED: 2026-06-13\nDOMAIN: apnews.com\nSLUG: russia-ukraine-war-drone-attack-a2189d216731d92cbe74c873e1e6c04e\nTEXT: A drone attack on a Black Sea export terminal in Russia\'s Volgograd region damaged oil transportation infrastructure. Ukrainian forces hit an oil preparation and pumping station in the same region, as well as Russian-occupied areas in Donetsk and Zaporizhzhia regions. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy stated that his forces had struck several military and energy infrastructure sites deep inside Russia, including a facility in Cheboksary that supplied components for Russian drones and missiles.\n\nID: 4189294\nCREATED: 2026-06-13\nDOMAIN: themoscowtimes.com\nSLUG: ukrainian-strike-kills-one-wounds-3-in-southern-russia-a93007\nTEXT: A Ukrainian drone strike in southern Russia\'s Temryuk district killed one person and wounded at least three others, with 96 people drafted to fight a fire caused by the attack. The strike damaged port installations near the Kerch Strait, which separates mainland Russia from occupied Crimea. Russian authorities reported shooting down 177 Ukrainian drones overnight, amid a recent surge in Ukrainian attacks within Russia.\n\nID: 4188992\nCREATED: 2026-06-13\nDOMAIN: fakti.bg\nSLUG: 1060716-russian-drones-attacked-sumy-nikolaev-and-zaporozhye-there-are-casualties-and-injuries\nTEXT: Russian drones attacked Sumy, Nikolaev, and Zaporozhye, resulting in casualties and injuries. The Ukrainian military reported that the drones entered through Chernihiv region along the border with Belarus, heading towards the northern part of Kyiv region. Separate groups of drones also flew over Poltava region, en route to Lubny city.\n\n\n',)
