etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4189835\nCREATED: 2026-06-13\nDOMAIN: gulftoday.ae\nSLUG: funeral-for-irans-late-supreme-leader-ayatollah-khamenei-to-begin-on-july-4-burial-set-for-july-9\nTEXT: Iran\'s funeral for late Supreme Leader Ayatollah Khamenei is set to begin on July 4, with a burial scheduled for July 9. Islamic law requires the deceased to be buried as soon as possible, ideally within 24 hours of death. The airstrike that killed Khamenei pulverised his central Tehran compound, where he was living. His 56-year-old son Mojtaba succeeded him as Supreme Leader after the airstrike, which also injured him and claimed his wife\'s life. Pakistan\'s Prime Minister Shahbaz Sharif announced that Iran and the US have agreed on a framework for a peace deal after three months of war, with an initial signing expected within 24 hours.\n\nID: 4189867\nCREATED: 2026-06-13\nDOMAIN: geo.tv\nSLUG: 668580-irans-late-supreme-leader-ali-khamenei-to-be-buried-on-july-9-state-tv\nTEXT: Iran\'s late Supreme Leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei will be buried on July 9 in his hometown of Mashhad, following three days of funeral ceremonies in Tehran and Qom. The burial was initially scheduled for March but postponed due to the war. Mojtaba Khamenei, Ali\'s son and successor as supreme leader, will not appear in public after his appointment.\n\nID: 4189901\nCREATED: 2026-06-13\nDOMAIN: thecitizen.co.tz\nSLUG: iran-s-supreme-leader-khamenei-burial-set-for-july-9-four-months-after-he-was-killed-in-february-5495072\nTEXT: Iran\'s Supreme Leader Khamenei burial set for July 9, four months after his death in February. According to Pakistani media, Prime Minister Shehbaz Sharif announced that Iran and the United States have agreed on a framework for a peace deal, with an initial agreement expected to be signed within 24 hours.\n\nID: 4189647\nCREATED: 2026-06-13\nDOMAIN: ctvnews.ca\nSLUG: funeral-for-irans-supreme-leader-set-for-july-while-a-deal-nears-to-end-the-war\nTEXT: Funeral for Iran\'s Supreme Leader set for July, a deal nears to end the war. \n\nIran\'s Supreme Leader Khamenei has died, and a funeral is set for July. The death comes amid ongoing tensions with the US over the war in Yemen. \n\nA deal to end the war is nearing, but details are not available.\n\nID: 4189891\nCREATED: 2026-06-13\nDOMAIN: africanews.com\nSLUG: iran-to-bury-late-supreme-leader-khamenei-on-july-9\nTEXT: Iran plans to bury the late Supreme Leader Khamenei on July 9. Mojtaba Khamenei, the wounded son of the deceased leader, has not appeared in public since his appointment and communicates only through statements attributed to him.\n\n\n',)
