etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4189482\nCREATED: 2026-06-13\nDOMAIN: prnewswire.com\nSLUG: as-the-lights-fade-vivid-sydney-2026-leaves-the-city-glowing-302798982-html\nTEXT: Vivid Sydney Festival Director Brett Sheehy AO praised the 2026 festival as an "extraordinary success", with visitors attending 4.5 locations on average and spending three hours immersed in the festival per visit. The festival featured spectacular aerial performances, sculpture and visual arts elements, and blockbuster laser and pyrotechnic shows. Kia presented its fifth consecutive year as a Major Partner with the "Kia Refraction" installation in Bligh & Barney Reserve, while Samsung activated for its fifth year as a partner with an immersive, interactive sculptural installation in First Fleet Park. Lilly Australia joined as an Official Partner, celebrating its 150th anniversary with a Vivid Minds panel, and Uber came on board as an Official Partner with dedicated pick-up and drop-off zones across the festival footprint.\n\nID: 4189480\nCREATED: 2026-06-13\nDOMAIN: prnewswire.com\nSLUG: al-caer-la-noche-vivid-sydney-2026-deja-la-ciudad-resplandeciente-302799449-html\nTEXT: Vivid Sydney 2026 sets a new record for attendance and enthusiasm, with visitors exploring more than ever before. The festival saw an increase in participation across all programs, with attendees visiting 4.5 locations on average and spending around three hours at each visit. Kia, Samsung Electronics Australia, and IREN returned as main sponsors for 2026, with Kia presenting its fifth consecutive year as a sponsor and Samsung renewing its partnership for the fifth time. Lilly Australia joined as an official sponsor, celebrating 150 years and presenting a panel on "Vivid Minds" titled "A new horizon for health". Uber also partnered as an official sponsor, offering exclusive pickup and delivery zones throughout the festival grounds.\n\n\n',)
